<title>INDONESIA: Rig Tender soars on takeover talk.</title>
<headline>Rig Tender soars on takeover talk.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian shipping firm Rig Tender soared on Tuesday following market talk that the company would be taken over by a foreign firm, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;I heard one foreign firm will take over the company but we could not get confirmation,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Rig Tender rose 75 rupiah to 1,475 rupiah in early trade but then eased to 1,450 rupiah on a volume of 2.4 million shares in the afternoon session. Trading volumes were the highest on the board.</p>
<p>Company officials denied the rumours.</p>
<p>&quot;It is baseless, we do not have such a plan or anything to do with foreign partnership,&quot; said a company official, who declined to speculate on the reasons for the rise in the share price.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
